{
  "table": "Appendix 11. Tables of acceptable measurement ranges of observed variables as a function of depth and basin",
  "source": "World Ocean Database 2023 User's Manual (knowledge/wod_readme.pdf)",
  "pages": "87-113",
  "what_this_is": "The manual gives min/max per depth level for each ocean basin (up to 30 basin columns per variable). Placing a cast in a basin needs the range_area.msk and range_basin_list.msk files from the WOD website, so these values are the union across basins: the lowest minimum and the highest maximum at each depth.",
  "consequence": "Depth-dependent but permissive: marginal seas widen it (at 5500 m salinity spans 1.0-50.0, from the Baltic and the Red Sea). A value inside it may still be outside its own basin's range.",
  "lookup_rule": "A depth between two listed levels uses the nearest listed level; if equidistant, the shallower one (manual p.86). The deepest entry, 5500, covers all greater depths.",
